Dear Mitsuko,

Thank you for the reading with Ishikawa this afternoon. I have attached my note on the 09:00 table.

As we discussed at 14:00, please keep the two descriptions separate on the page. For progress, show the 31 of 48 planned participants with a first observation in the implementation ledger alongside the 17 not yet observed. The latter should not be assigned to the missing reasons in the item rows.

For recording status, use the eligible denominator for each item and describe the records present and the reasons for missing entries within that set. In particular, the response-date row is 8 recorded out of 12 issued query rows, with four awaiting confirmation. Those are query rows, not participants. Four items with missing entries do not imply four participants with missing data.

For the research meeting, please limit the presentation to progress and the interim recording status supported by the records at the 20 January 09:00 cutoff. We cannot draw a between-group conclusion from this table; the pending queries can be followed up for the next cut.

Best regards,
Koichi Goto
Yoshimura Statistics LLC

On 20 January 2026 at 11:36, Mitsuko Suzuki wrote:
> Dear Koichi,
>
> Before our 14:00 reading today, could you look at Ishikawa's attached v0.2 table and help me with two points?
>
> First, I propose putting the progress from the implementation ledger in a separate field: as of 09:00 on 20 January, initial observation has been completed for 31 of the 48 planned participants. The remaining 17 have not yet been observed. How should we explain those 17 when reading the table, so that they are not mistaken for missing records within an item?
>
> Second, four items have at least one missing entry among their respective eligible records. I propose describing these as item-level recording status, separately from progress. The first three items are counted in participants, while the response-date item is counted in issued query rows. Could you check whether this distinction and the item-specific denominators are clear enough for the meeting material?
>
> The attached table is KRC-LDO-20260120-TAB-001 v0.2, using the 09:00 cutoff. I would like to keep our description to what the records at that point support.
>
> Thank you, and see you this afternoon.
>
> Best regards,
> Mitsuko Suzuki
> Katsuragawa Clinical Research Center

